Hello, 

that's basically the idea, yes. The global/local tests are not great. They have good type 1 error but lack power. If one is significant, then definitely you can look at global/local components of sPCA, but that won't tell you how many to retain. If it is not significant, then... it is not really helping, as you don't know if this is lack of power or just absence of structure.

Cheers

Thibaut

